\title{gAtoms: structural graph decomposition}
\description{
Decomposes simple undirected graphs using a C implementation of recursive atom decomposition and clique minimal separator expansion with the igraph C library. Provides deterministic perfect orderings, component trees, vertex mappings, residuals and validated structural S3 objects for sparse or dense graph inputs. Fits fixed-graph Gaussian concentration models by combining local atom estimates and complete separator estimates. Fits graphical log-linear models from categorical observations using local sufficient margins and factorized distributions without a global table. Computes decomposition-aware G-Wishart log normalizing constants, using exact closed forms for complete prime components and clique separators and optional BDgraph Monte Carlo for incomplete prime components.
